An exported import alias, `export import Name = Namespace.member`, is listed as `export import` and the alias name, like an unexported one; the grammar parses it as an `import_alias` inside the `export` statement.
- `export import R = require('r')` doesn't parse as an alias in this grammar version, but its name is still listed, as `export import R`.
== args
input/aliases.ts
== file input/aliases.ts
export import Join = path.join;
import fs = require('fs');
export import R = require('r');
== stdout
input/aliases.ts (3 lines)
[L1-L1] export import Join
[L2-L2] import fs
[L3-L3] export import R
